.TH "AIU_SHELL_JUMP" "1" "2021-04-12" "" "aiu-shell-jump"
.SH NAME
\fBaiu-shell-jump-init\fR - generate shell configuration for aiu-shell-jump
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aiu-shell-jump init SHELL [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
To initialize aiu-shell-jump on your shell:
.TP
.B bash
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (usually \fB~/.bashrc\fR):
.sp
.nf
    \fBeval "$(aiu-shell-jump init bash)"\fR
.fi
.TP
.B elvish
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (usually \fB~/.elvish/rc.elv\fR):
.sp
.nf
    \fBeval $(aiu-shell-jump init elvish | slurp)\fR
.fi
.sp
Note: aiu-shell-jump only supports elvish v0.18.0 and above.
.TP
.B fish
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (usually
\fB~/.config/fish/config.fish\fR):
.sp
.nf
    \fBaiu-shell-jump init fish | source\fR
.fi
.TP
.B nushell
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your env file (find it by running
\fB$nu.env-path\fR in Nushell):
.sp
.nf
    \fBaiu-shell-jump init nushell | save -f ~/.aiu-shell-jump.nu\fR
.fi
.sp
Now, add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (find it by running
\fB$nu.config-path\fR in Nushell):
.sp
.nf
    \fBsource ~/.aiu-shell-jump.nu\fR
.fi
.sp
Note: aiu-shell-jump only supports Nushell v0.89.0+.
.TP
.B powershell
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (find it by running \fBecho
$profile\fR in PowerShell):
.sp
.nf
    \fBInvoke-Expression (& { (aiu-shell-jump init powershell | Out-String) })\fR
.fi
.TP
.B tcsh
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (usually \fB~/.tcshrc\fR):
.sp
.nf
    \fBaiu-shell-jump init tcsh > ~/.aiu-shell-jump.tcsh\fR
    \fBsource ~/.aiu-shell-jump.tcsh\fR
.fi
.TP
.B xonsh
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (usually \fB~/.xonshrc\fR):
.sp
.nf
    \fBexecx($(aiu-shell-jump init xonsh), 'exec', __xonsh__.ctx, filename='aiu-shell-jump')\fR
.fi
.TP
.B zsh
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file (usually \fB~/.zshrc\fR):
.sp
.nf
    \fBeval "$(aiu-shell-jump init zsh)"\fR
.fi
.TP
.B any POSIX shell
.sp
Add this to the \fBend\fR of your config file:
.sp
.nf
    \fBeval "$(aiu-shell-jump init posix --hook prompt)"\fR
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --cmd
Changes the prefix of the \fBz\fR and \fBzi\fR commands.
.br
\fB--cmd j\fR would change the commands to (\fBj\fR, \fBji\fR).
.br
\fB--cmd cd\fR would replace the \fBcd\fR command (doesn't work on Nushell /
POSIX shells).
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help information.
.TP
.B --hook HOOK
Changes how often aiu-shell-jump increments a directory's score:
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
    \fBnone\fR|Never
    \fBprompt\fR|At every shell prompt
    \fBpwd\fR|Whenever the directory is changed
.TE
.TP
.B --no-cmd
Prevents aiu-shell-jump from defining the \fBz\fR and \fBzi\fR commands. These functions
will still be available in your shell as \fB__aiu_shell_jump_z\fR and \fB__aiu_shell_jump_zi\fR,
should you choose to redefine them.
